","side":"away","factor":1.098,"effect_pct":8.2,"measured_pct":3.9,"detail":"SC Cambuur shots on target in last 6: 34 for (expected 29.2); FC Utrecht conceded 38 (expected 31.6)","status":"measured"}],"sample":{"home_games":51,"away_games":5,"home_all":102,"away_all":12},"basis":{"min_games":5,"team_news":true},"h2h":[],"analyst_view":{"overall":"Struggling Utrecht (14th, 12 pts) host promoted Cambuur (10th, 15 pts), who went seven unbeaten before a 5-2 home loss to PSV before the break. Utrecht lost their last two league games (Telstar, NEC), have conceded 34 goals in 12 games, and coach Anthony Correia is under heavy pressure with fan banners at the training ground; he says the plan stays but the gaps between the lines must shrink. Jonathans and Ohio are out long term; Correia said today that Engwanda, Paredes and Jensen are back in the group but not yet match-fit, so at most they could come off the bench, while the numbers count them as out. Cambuur's main threat is Utrecht loanee Rafik El Arguioui; they miss Amofa, Visser and Westerhof, Asselman is still unlikely, and Sports Mole expects Jansen in goal. Referee Allard Lindhout (3.2 cards a game) is already counted.","goals":{"lean":"higher","adjust_pct":3,"call":"Around 4.2 goals","text":"The numbers say 4.1 goals, already counting Cambuur's scoring run (16 in six) and Utrecht's leaky defence (15 conceded in six). Correia himself points to the gaps behind his midfield, El Arguioui is in form against his parent club, and Cambuur are expected to use their reserve keeper Jansen, which the numbers give no goal effect; a mild +3% to about 4.2."},"corners":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 9.8 corners","text":"The numbers say 9.8 corners, most of them Utrecht's (6.4). A Utrecht side under pressure at home should push forward while Cambuur sit in and counter, but that is already the shape of the numbers, so I stay at 9.8."},"cards":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 4.0 cards","text":"The numbers s